# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows checks out CRLF by default, and `rustfmt.toml` pins
# `newline_style = "Unix"` — so `cargo fmt --check` passed on the machine the files were
# written on and failed on a Windows CI runner that had converted them. The check was
# right and the repository was ambiguous.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `text=auto`: auto guesses per file, and a guess is what produced
# the disagreement in the first place.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched. An icon with its newlines "normalised" is a corrupt icon.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.db binary
*.bundle binary

# Recorded RPC responses and ABI calldata are compared byte for byte by tests.
*.hex -text
crates/chain/tests/fixtures/** -text

# Generated; keep them out of diffs and out of language statistics.
Cargo.lock linguist-generated=true
ui/package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
